<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="OBA" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Obadiah</para>
  <para style="mt">Obadiah</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The vision of ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>. Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> concerning Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>; We have heard a rumour from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and an ambassador is sent among the heathen, Arise you<char style="ord">2f</char>, and let us rise up against her in battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Behold, I have made you<char style="ord">i</char> small among the heathen: you<char style="ord">i</char> are greatly despised.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The pride of your<char style="ord">i</char> heart has deceived you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> that dwell in the clefts of the rock, whose habitation <char style="add">[is]</char> high; that says in his heart, Who shall bring me down to the ground?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Though you<char style="ord">i</char> exalt <char style="add">[yourself]</char> as the eagle, and though you<char style="ord">i</char> set your<char style="ord">i</char> nest among the stars, there will I bring you<char style="ord">i</char> down, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />If thieves came to you<char style="ord">i</char>, if robbers by night, <char style="pn">(how are you<char style="ord">i</char> cut off!)</char> would they not have stolen till they had enough? if the grapegatherers came to you<char style="ord">i</char>, would they not leave <char style="add">[some]</char> grapes?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />How are <char style="add">[the things]</char> of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char> searched out! <char style="add">[how]</char> are his hidden things sought up!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />All the men of your<char style="ord">i</char> alliance have brought you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[even]</char> to the border: the men that were at peace with you<char style="ord">i</char> have deceived you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> prevailed against you<char style="ord">i</char>; <char style="add">[they that eat]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> bread have laid a wound under you<char style="ord">i</char>: <char style="add">[there is]</char> none understanding in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Shall I not in that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, even destroy the wise <char style="add">[men]</char> out of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and understanding out of the mount of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And your<char style="ord">i</char> mighty <char style="add">[men]</char>, O Teman <char style="add">[south]</char>, shall be dismayed, to the end that every one of the mount of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char> may be cut off by slaughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> violence against you<char style="ord">i</char> brother Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> shame shall cover you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be cut off forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />In the day that you<char style="ord">i</char> stood on the other side, in the day that the strangers carried away captive his forces, and foreigners entered into his gates, and cast lots upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, even you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> as one of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">i</char> should not have looked on the day of your<char style="ord">i</char> brother in the day that he became a stranger; neither should you<char style="ord">i</char> have rejoiced over the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> in the day of their destruction; neither should you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken proudly in the day of distress.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> should not have entered into the gate of my people in the day of their calamity; yes, you<char style="ord">i</char> should not have looked on their affliction in the day of their calamity, nor have laid <char style="add">[hands]</char> on their substance in the day of their calamity;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Neither should you<char style="ord">i</char> have stood in the crossway, to cut off those of his that did escape; neither should you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered up those of his that did remain in the day of distress.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> near upon all the heathen: as you<char style="ord">i</char> have done, it shall be done unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: your<char style="ord">i</char> reward shall return upon your<char style="ord">i</char> own head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have drunk upon my holy mountain, <char style="add">[so]</char> shall all the heathen drink continually, yes, they shall drink, and they shall swallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> down, and they shall be as though they had not been.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But upon mount Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char> shall be deliverance, and there shall be holiness; and the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> shall possess their possessions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> shall be a fire, and the house of Yosef <char style="pn">[(God) He Shall Add]</char> a flame, and the house of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char> for stubble, and they shall kindle in them, and devour them; and there shall not be <char style="add">[any]</char> remaining of the house of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And <char style="add">[they of]</char> the south shall possess the mount of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char>; and <char style="add">[they of]</char> the plain the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and they shall possess the fields of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and the fields of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>: and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength] [shall possess]</char> Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the captivity of this host of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [shall possess]</char> that of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto Tzarfat <char style="add">[refinery]</char>; and the captivity of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in S’farad <char style="add">[separated]</char>, shall possess the cities of the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And saviours shall come up on mount Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char> to judge the mount of ‘Esav <char style="add">[Hairy]</char>; and the kingdom shall be the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>.</para>
</usx>